.TH UPTIME 1 Nexix
.SH NAME
uptime \- time since boot, logged-in sessions and scheduler load
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uptime
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the current local time, elapsed boot time, logged-in user session count,
and the 1-, 5- and 15-minute load averages.
Boot time uses monotonic kernel ticks and is independent of date changes.
Each occupied utmp entry counts as one session, including multiple sessions
belonging to the same user.
.PP
Load averages are exponentially damped samples taken once per second.
They count runnable user processes and uninterruptible I/O waits.
Stopped processes, zombies, interruptible sleeps, timed sleeps and kernel
system processes do not contribute.
Averages start at zero at boot; they are not normalized by CPU count.
.PP
This command and the kernel load samples are native Nexix extensions.
.SH SEE ALSO
ps(1), who(1), date(1)
